# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the disaggregation step-1 window (docs/tp4-disagg-step1.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/disagg and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry. Templates only.
# D3: today's TP4 production stack (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic: fast path, Lever N, W2, engine reuse, prefix reuse) on the same image and prompts:
# the absolute TP4 prefill at 4k/32k/128k/250k (1x258000 nominal is about 244-250k as the server counts it, under the profile's 253,920 cap) and decode per seat at 1/2/4/8 live
# (4k) and 8 live at 32k, which the model scales by D1/D2's r and k to estimate a TP2 fast-path pair; stall8_cold128k is the decoders' rate INSIDE a cold 120k prefill window,
# the interference a separate prefill pair would remove. concurrent8_steady is named because the profile asks for the eight-seat quad (c2_serving_job.steady_eight_problems).
# Unsalted bench requests never hit the prefix cache, so every prefill here is cold. READ: bench-<profile>.json, the stall8_cold128k line (arrival_ttft_s, worst_gap_s, window),
# concurrent8_steady, c2_smoke_check clean. Duration (estimate): reset 3-12 min, engine load 11-14 min, bench ~25 min, stall ~6 min, steady ~8 min: 55-75 min (box 120).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,bench,stall8_cold128k,concurrent8_steady
C2_BENCH_SHAPES=1x4096,1x32768,1x131072,1x258000,2x4096,4x4096,8x4096,8x32768
C2_BOX_MINUTES=120
